{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1145149-mage-2ed-status-in-caucus-and-concilium-and-in-chicago-1ed","id":1145149,"title":"[Mage 2ed] Status in Caucus and Concilium and in Chicago 1ed","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-09-29T03:25:09-07:00","id":1145149,"title":"[Mage 2ed] Status in Caucus and Concilium and in Chicago 1ed","content":"I\u00b4m currently working on again on a Mage campaign set in Chicago as described in the CofD 1ed book. <br /> Of course I have some confusing details to think about (for example: Status Merits are quite lazy scattered over the characters and sometimes are contradicting the described Status)<br /> <br /> How do you use the Social Status merits and furthermore how do you use the order specific titles? <br /> <br /> I recognize Concilum Status as this, and it\u00b4s easy to give every character the Concilium Status as described. <br /> <br /> X- Nonmember of the local concilum<br /> 1 - Rising Star / Vassal<br /> 2 - Sentinels / Heralds / Interfector <br /> 3 - Provost<br /> 4 - Councilor<br /> 5 - Hierarch<br /> <br /> But more importantly, as the role of the order caucus changed - and became more important as a political body i was thinking about the Status of the characters from the book. Many don\u00b4t have any Status at all, even though they are described as seniour members of their order. <br /> How do you handle a low order status but a high concilium Status. For the GotV it\u00b4s simple as the Epopt is many times secret - in My chicago it\u00b4s Taliesin (who actually has GotV Status of 4, which is higher than Manipra - but he\u00b4s still not the Leader of the whole Caucus.<br /> <br /> My Chicago Concilium<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Hierarch: Manipra (Guardians of the Veil) (Concilium 4 (Hierarch) &amp; GotV 3)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Councilor 1 \u2014 Adamantine Arrow: Deathsong (Not described or &quot;Stated&quot;) as she is a member in a GotV i picked her as an easy and quite pro GotV AdA Councilor</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Councilor 2 \u2014 Silver Ladder: Altus Vulcanis (Councilor -with Status 5!)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Councilor 3 \u2014 Mysterium: Libra (Concilium Status 2 - but no title? , No Myst Status)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Councilor 4 \u2014 Free Council: Laplace (Described as both Leader of the FC and councilor, but no Merit-Dots in Status)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Provost (Hierarch\u2019s): Saena (Guardians of the Veil) (Described as Provost - but only her GotV Status of 2 is given)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Provost (Adamantine Arrow): </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Princess Kundalini (Just for fun and to give the Abatoir more politcal clout without pushing the Chevalier</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Provost (Silver Ladder): L\u2019Etranger (Provost 4!)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Provost (Mysterium): Melpomene (Maybe to political as a position and maybe changing it with Rose\u00b4s) </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Provost (Free Council): Southpaw (Concilium Status 4 - but no description whatsoever about it), FC just 1)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Herald 1: Rose (Maybe a different character... but who?)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Herald 2: Triplex ( Herald - 2, Has only FC Status 2 (as a Cabal Leader - funny - other Caballeaders don\u00b4t have this)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Sentinel 1: Chevalier (Described as Sentinel but has Status 3, no AA Status)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Sentinel 2: Mimir (Described as Muscle and maybe Sentinel - but no Status)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Sentinel 3: Kid Chaillot (never to be seen <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )</span></span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Gamelines: Requiem, Lost, Awakening, Trinity Continuum: Aeon, some V5.<br /> Likes cheesecake (quark-based)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1305-maekkel","name":"maekkel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1305_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-29T03:57:08-07:00","id":1145155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>maekkel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1145149-mage-2ed-status-in-caucus-and-concilium-and-in-chicago-1ed#post1145149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u00b4m currently working on again on a Mage campaign set in Chicago as described in the CofD 1ed book.<br /> Of course I have some confusing details to think about (for example: Status Merits are quite lazy scattered over the characters and sometimes are contradicting the described Status)<br /> <br /> How do you use the Social Status merits and furthermore how do you use the order specific titles?<br /> <br /> Snip</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Honestly, i wouldnt put that much work into it for NPC chars, as long as you know what they are and stuff, actual dots dont really matter. If your PC's started investing exp in status / working to get more then you might need to work out how they compare to the npc's but really, the merit points are just there for PC's to get cool shit with. Maybe im just lazy though, but i have been burnt by putting lots of effort into something my players had no interest in before so now i do as little as possible until they show interest in something.<br /> <br /> tldr: wing it till it matters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-29T04:30:51-07:00","id":1145164,"title":"","content":"You are right about winging it. <br /> I\u00b4m also more concerned about the canon characters which are published in books, which is sometimes confusing when you read through the character and then only discover in their merit list that they hold a actual political title in their concilium and/or caucus. <br /> <br /> Also - I building the city and have statted characters so that maybe other ST/players might use them and we have a common ground.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Gamelines: Requiem, Lost, Awakening, Trinity Continuum: Aeon, some V5.<br /> Likes cheesecake (quark-based)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1305-maekkel","name":"maekkel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1305_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}